WEBVTT

00:01.570 --> 00:04.260
I'm still wondering why I have to be executed.

00:04.260 --> 00:06.490
It's your fault!

00:06.490 --> 00:08.660
I don't want to regret the way I lived!

00:08.660 --> 00:13.740
But what are you going to do when someone 
you saved kills someone else in the future?

00:14.100 --> 00:17.370
When you die, you should 
be surrounded by people.

00:17.370 --> 00:21.100
It's been decided that you'll 
be secretly executed.

00:21.100 --> 00:24.520
I've already decided how I'm going to die.

00:25.370 --> 00:30.920
That would mean people cursed me 
and my mom with those hearts!

00:30.920 --> 00:32.760
What is a proper death?

00:33.940 --> 00:36.650
The value of life would become ambiguous...

00:37.010 --> 00:40.210
I wouldn't even understand the importance 
of those I care about anymore.

00:40.780 --> 00:42.270
And that scares me.

00:43.010 --> 00:45.260
It's your fault!

00:45.260 --> 00:48.700
When you die, you should 
be surrounded by people.

00:48.700 --> 00:50.710
Help others.

00:50.710 --> 00:53.030
Guess I can't afford to die now.

00:53.810 --> 00:58.860
So I've never once regretted saving you.

00:58.860 --> 01:01.260
We're accomplices.

01:01.260 --> 01:02.620
I won't...

01:03.210 --> 01:04.260
lose again.

01:04.850 --> 01:07.040
Then I'm gonna win.

01:07.040 --> 01:08.690
Apologize...

01:08.690 --> 01:10.810
to my brothers in the afterlife!

01:10.810 --> 01:13.060
You're a strong kid, so help others.

01:13.060 --> 01:16.030
Are you ready to witness it, Itadori-kun?

01:16.030 --> 01:18.640
People die. There's no stopping that.

01:18.640 --> 01:21.240
So I wanted them to at 
least have proper deaths.

01:21.240 --> 01:26.000
Are you going to blame your grandfather 
when you're killed by a curse, too?

01:26.000 --> 01:29.910
...and have lots of them 
watching over me when I die.

01:30.250 --> 01:33.760
But tears were shed over 
the lives I ended tonight.

01:33.760 --> 01:36.740
People are going to die because you live!

01:40.990 --> 01:43.990
Episode 42
Right and Wrong

01:54.550 --> 01:59.070
JUJUTSU KAISEN
Shibuya Incident

04:54.080 --> 04:56.030
Malaysia...

04:57.560 --> 04:59.240
Yeah...

04:59.240 --> 05:01.070
Malaysia...

05:01.570 --> 05:03.320
Kuantan would be nice.

05:03.910 --> 05:07.170
I'll build a home on a secluded beach.

05:07.660 --> 05:11.300
I already have a mountain of books 
that I've bought and never touched.

05:12.020 --> 05:14.000
I'll read through them page by page,

05:14.470 --> 05:17.990
like I'm taking back all the time I've lost.

05:18.830 --> 05:20.390
No.

05:20.390 --> 05:24.380
Right now, I'm going to save Fushiguro-kun...

05:25.080 --> 05:26.730
And Maki-san?

05:27.080 --> 05:28.840
What about Naobito-san?

05:29.120 --> 05:31.040
What happened to those two?

05:34.800 --> 05:37.120
I'm tired.

05:37.120 --> 05:38.890
Exhausted, even.

05:39.460 --> 05:41.610
Yeah, I'm exhausted.

05:44.530 --> 05:47.270
I've already done enough.

08:10.000 --> 08:11.870
You're here?

08:14.120 --> 08:17.700
I've been here. The whole time.

08:26.500 --> 08:28.410
You're here?

08:29.840 --> 08:32.630
I've been here. The whole time.

08:32.970 --> 08:35.000
Shall we chat for a bit?

08:35.710 --> 08:38.630
You and I have gone at it 
a few times, after all.

08:45.970 --> 08:52.070
Haibara, what was I even hoping 
to accomplish in the end?

08:52.070 --> 08:53.640
I ran.

08:54.270 --> 08:59.100
I ran away, and yet I came back over 
some vague reason like a job worth doing.

09:07.670 --> 09:09.210
I can't.

09:10.210 --> 09:11.830
That's wrong.

09:18.210 --> 09:20.400
I can't, Haibara.

09:22.840 --> 09:24.780
I can't say that.

09:24.780 --> 09:27.750
It'll just become a curse upon him.

09:32.650 --> 09:33.880
Nanamin...

09:46.480 --> 09:47.820
I shouldn't.

09:52.100 --> 09:53.200
I sh—

10:01.310 --> 10:02.850
Itadori-kun.

10:19.680 --> 10:21.610
You take it from here.

10:47.320 --> 10:48.190
Wha—

10:51.680 --> 10:53.300
What the hell...

10:55.880 --> 11:00.010
What the hell are you, Mahito?!

11:00.010 --> 11:03.370
You don't have to shout! I can hear you!

11:03.370 --> 11:05.880
Yuji Itadori!

11:20.490 --> 11:22.540
Save me!

11:28.160 --> 11:29.860
Save me!

11:31.170 --> 11:33.420
Save me!

11:37.920 --> 11:39.420
Soul Multiplicity!

11:40.770 --> 11:42.090
Body Repel!

12:15.320 --> 12:17.650
If only I'd used a little more force,

12:17.650 --> 12:20.040
I could've stabbed through your face.

12:23.600 --> 12:26.880
How can you possibly

12:26.880 --> 12:29.160
toy with countless

12:29.160 --> 12:32.730
people's lives over and over?!

12:37.680 --> 12:41.940
Would you be satisfied if I counted each 
one off my fingers with a look of regret?

12:42.580 --> 12:44.270
I'll start doing that with the next one.

12:45.270 --> 12:49.800
I'll grant you a simple answer 
since you're such a simple guy.

12:50.790 --> 12:52.600
Yuji Itadori.

12:55.200 --> 12:57.640
Help me!

13:00.590 --> 13:02.490
You are me.

13:03.640 --> 13:05.020
Huh?!

13:05.020 --> 13:07.310
Quit snapping at everything.

13:07.310 --> 13:09.430
It's just a curse's nonsense, right?

13:13.280 --> 13:14.540
However,

13:15.440 --> 13:17.990
until you're willing to accept that,

13:21.340 --> 13:23.450
you can't beat me.

13:23.880 --> 13:25.690
On and on...

13:25.950 --> 13:27.880
You talk a lot.

13:27.880 --> 13:29.350
Those your dying words?

13:30.310 --> 13:32.300
You take it from here.

13:33.710 --> 13:38.180
Nanamin would never make the 
mistake of losing himself to anger.

13:39.110 --> 13:40.850
Prove it.

13:41.300 --> 13:42.460
You are...

13:41.300 --> 13:42.460
I am...

13:46.080 --> 13:47.670
...a jujutsu sorcerer.

15:44.500 --> 15:47.000
Nice. Let's keep going.

15:49.500 --> 15:52.010
Time for round two!

15:54.370 --> 15:57.030
JUJUTSU KAISEN

15:54.370 --> 15:57.030
JUJUTSU KAISEN

16:00.000 --> 16:02.040
JUJUTSU KAISEN

16:00.000 --> 16:02.040
JUJUTSU KAISEN

16:02.040 --> 16:03.520
23:19        Shibuya Station, Dogenzaka Ticket Gate

18:12.370 --> 18:13.560
Too close!

18:13.980 --> 18:17.110
If I pick the wrong moments 
to take risks, I'll die.

18:17.110 --> 18:20.240
I guess I'll attack mostly with
transfigured humans for a while.

18:20.240 --> 18:21.780
Oh, how scary.

18:22.100 --> 18:24.290
He has even more tricks than before.

18:33.330 --> 18:34.340
A kid?!

18:34.340 --> 18:36.340
Hey! Over here!

18:36.340 --> 18:39.040
It's dangerous and full of 
monsters over there!

18:39.040 --> 18:41.040
It's...

18:41.040 --> 18:42.380
upstairs?!

18:44.000 --> 18:45.110
Sorry.

18:45.470 --> 18:49.060
There's no safe place in Shibuya right now, 
so get as far away as you—

18:51.570 --> 18:54.060
Shit! That bastard!

19:03.080 --> 19:04.790
Come on now.

19:04.790 --> 19:05.740
Huh?

19:06.740 --> 19:09.760
Are you sure your imagination isn't stunted?

19:10.110 --> 19:10.750
Stop it!

19:11.010 --> 19:12.510
Are you an idiot?

19:12.510 --> 19:14.400
That all depends on you.

19:14.940 --> 19:18.720
This is the most effective tool 
against Itadori's mental state.

19:18.720 --> 19:20.200
Plus...

19:20.200 --> 19:24.760
We have one more card for insurance.

19:25.520 --> 19:26.120
Huh?!

19:26.120 --> 19:27.220
What?!

19:27.220 --> 19:28.520
Hey!

19:28.880 --> 19:30.800
Yeah, drink, drink, drink them up!

19:30.800 --> 19:32.230
Drink, drink, drink them up!

19:32.230 --> 19:33.720
Drink, drink, drink them up!

19:33.720 --> 19:34.920
Drink away!

19:35.770 --> 19:40.800
21:30        Shibuya Station, B4F

19:36.960 --> 19:38.140
Yay!

19:38.140 --> 19:40.220
I have plenty stocked up already,

19:40.220 --> 19:42.900
so you can do whatever you want 
with the people on floor B5.

19:42.900 --> 19:46.050
Okay, time to recommence 
the "Let's Kill Itadori" show!

19:46.050 --> 19:47.630
Burp!

19:47.630 --> 19:48.630
No!

19:48.630 --> 19:50.040
Jogo.

19:50.530 --> 19:52.320
Catch me if you can!

19:52.900 --> 19:53.800
Wha—

19:55.120 --> 19:56.550
I'll take the underground.

19:56.550 --> 19:58.980
You wander around the surface.

19:58.980 --> 20:01.130
Just come back when I call you.

20:01.130 --> 20:03.690
I know. You don't have to say it.

20:03.690 --> 20:05.260
I guess so.

20:07.140 --> 20:07.760
He split
into two!!

20:07.140 --> 20:07.760
He split
into two!!

20:08.240 --> 20:09.770
Bye-bye!

20:11.010 --> 20:13.020
Boing!

20:11.080 --> 20:13.020
Boing!

20:15.740 --> 20:17.190
He got away.

20:21.860 --> 20:24.860
Mahito!

20:24.860 --> 20:32.870
23:16        Dogenzaka Alleys

20:25.940 --> 20:27.750
Did you see that earlier?

20:27.750 --> 20:29.400
That was crazy, right?

20:29.400 --> 20:32.520
I was just wandering around 
that area not long ago, too.

20:33.120 --> 20:34.790
Patch-face...

20:34.790 --> 20:36.100
Was it you?

20:36.100 --> 20:39.890
Are you the special-grade cursed spirit 
that's been messing with our idiot?

20:40.380 --> 20:42.200
Well, jeez.

20:42.200 --> 20:44.120
Am I famous?

20:44.120 --> 20:45.040
Yeah.

20:45.040 --> 20:47.770
I heard you ran with your 
tail between your legs.

20:49.360 --> 20:50.580
I like you.

20:51.020 --> 20:53.060
You seem worth killing.

20:53.360 --> 20:56.640
I haven't had any good 
chances to shine today...

20:57.880 --> 21:02.050
They said this thing's technique 
had something to do with souls,

21:02.050 --> 21:04.560
and not to let its hands touch me, right?

21:05.600 --> 21:08.810
...so I'll have to settle for 
exorcising a cowardly bug like you.

21:09.460 --> 21:10.830
Recall it.

21:11.190 --> 21:15.210
Recall the essence of cursed energy 
that you seized back then!

21:17.420 --> 21:18.940
No control.

21:28.160 --> 21:29.680
Hairpin.

21:37.590 --> 21:38.880
Not bad.

21:39.160 --> 21:42.230
But in general, that won't work on me.

21:42.790 --> 21:44.850
Judging from what she said,

21:44.850 --> 21:47.360
she must be close to that guy.

21:47.770 --> 21:50.710
I'll drag this woman's corpse

21:50.710 --> 21:54.040
before Yuji Itadori and break his soul!

23:25.520 --> 23:27.170
Time for a personality test!

23:27.170 --> 23:29.880
Can you more clearly recall 
the person you used to love

23:29.880 --> 23:31.360
or the person you used to hate?

23:31.360 --> 23:33.140
Results after the title!

23:33.140 --> 23:35.200
Next time, "Right and Wrong, Part 2."

23:33.260 --> 23:39.930
Next Episode
Right and Wrong, Part 2

23:35.200 --> 23:39.750
Dwelling on the past means you're an otaku!
